  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>&#969;</mi></math> be a complex number such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></math> where <math><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> . If<br /><br /><math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo></math><br /><br />Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> can be equal to:",
    "image": null
